<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · concept</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sovereignty</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as territorial sovereignty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sovereignty is supreme political authority over a territory and its people, free from external control. The modern idea of territorial sovereignty is often linked to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-westphalia">Peace of Westphalia</a>, as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a> profile notes. Questions of sovereignty appear across many profiles, including those of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-shogunate">Tokugawa Shogunate</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate</a>, often as they faced foreign pressure.</p></div>
